    {
      "text": "Cyclotomic completions of polynomial rings — The main object of study in this paper is the completion Z[q]N = lim←− n Z[q]/ ((1− q)(1− q2)···(1− qn)) of the polynomial ring Z[q], which arises from\n\n**Cyclotomic completions of polynomial rings**\n\n18 pp, 24 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The main object of study in this paper is the completion Z[q]N = lim←− n Z[q]/ ((1− q)(1− q2)···(1− qn)) of the polynomial ring Z[q], which arises from the study of a new invariant of integral hom ology 3- spheres with values in Z[q]N announced by the author, which uniﬁes all the sl2 Witten-Reshetikhin-Turaev invariants at various roots of unity. We show that any element of Z[q]N is uniquely determined by its power series expansion in q− ζ for each root ζ of unity. We also show that any element of Z[q]N is uniquely determined by its values at the roots of unity. These results may be interpreted that Z[q]N behaves like a ring of “holomorphic functions deﬁned on the set of the roots of unity”.\n\n**Outline.** 2 KAZUO HABIRO; 1 Introduction; 4 KAZUO HABIRO; 2 Preliminaries; 6 KAZUO HABIRO; 3 Monic completions of polynomial rings; 3.1 Deﬁnitions and basic properties. For a rin; 3.2 Injectivity of the homomorphism ρR; 8 KAZUO HABIRO; 4 Injectivity of ρR; 10 KAZUO HABIRO; 5 Expansions at roots of unity; 12 KAZUO HABIRO; 6 V alues at roots of unity; 14 KAZUO HABIRO; 7 Remarks; 7.1 Units in Z[q]S. If R is a ring and S ⊂ MR ; 7.2 A localization of Z[q]N. In some applicati\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 4.2: states that if S′⊂ S⊂ N are subsets such that for any n∈ S\n- Theorem 3.4: If R is a ring and M0≺ M⊂M R, then the homomorphism\n- Theorem 3.4: Corollary 3.5. If R is a ring, and M ⊂M R is a ⇒R-connected subset,\n- Theorem 5.2: Let R be an integral domain of characteristic 0 and let Z⊂\n- Theorem 5.2: Theorem 5.4. Let R be an integral domain of characteristic 0, S⊂ N a\n- Theorem 6.1: Let R be a subring of the ﬁeld ¯Q of algebraic numbers,",
